   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "Origin\n\u2018Natsukaze\u2019 guinea grass has Plant Variety Rights\nprotection in Japan since November 1986. The\nbreeder is Hirosayu Sato, of Kyushu National\nAgricultural Experiment Station at Kumamoto,\nJapan.",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    62.4,
    164.16,
    272.16,
    263.52
   ],
   "id": "e3",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      62.88,
      164.16,
      267.36,
      172.8
     ],
     "text": "This variety arises from the controlled pollination"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      62.4,
      173.76,
      236.64,
      182.88
     ],
     "text": "of a sexual plant accession by pollen from"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      62.88,
      183.84,
      272.16,
      193.44
     ],
     "text": "apomictic accessions. Selection of sexual progeny"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      62.4,
      193.92,
      260.16,
      203.52
     ],
     "text": "was made for three generations, on the basis of"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      62.88,
      204.48,
      272.16,
      213.6
     ],
     "text": "early growth vigour and high dry matter yield. The"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      63.36,
      214.56,
      240.96,
      222.24
     ],
     "text": "resultant material was then evaluated at 13"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      62.88,
      224.64,
      272.16,
      233.76
     ],
     "text": "different sites in Japan from 1981 to 1984 for yield,"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      62.88,
      234.72,
      259.68,
      243.84
     ],
     "text": "chemical composition, nutrient value and other"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      62.88,
      244.32,
      266.4,
      253.92
     ],
     "text": "performance characteristics, resulting in the final"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      62.88,
      254.88,
      191.52,
      263.52
     ],
     "text": "selection of an apomictic plant."
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "This variety arises from the controlled pollination\nof a sexual plant accession by pollen from\napomictic accessions. Selection of sexual progeny\nwas made for three generations, on the basis of\nearly growth vigour and high dry matter yield. The\nresultant material was then evaluated at 13\ndifferent sites in Japan from 1981 to 1984 for yield,\nchemical composition, nutrient value and other\nperformance characteristics, resulting in the final\nselection of an apomictic plant.",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    296.16,
    48.96,
    508.32,
    96.96
   ],
   "id": "e4",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      296.16,
      48.96,
      458.4,
      58.08
     ],
     "text": "Morphology \u2014 See comparison tables."
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      296.64,
      58.56,
      508.32,
      67.68
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Natsukaze\u2019 is a perennial tetraploid (2n = 32) erect"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      296.16,
      68.64,
      486.72,
      78.72
     ],
     "text": "growing guinea grass. Its reproduction is 85%"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      296.64,
      78.72,
      508.32,
      88.8
     ],
     "text": "apomictic \u2014 that is, producing seed without sexual"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      297.12,
      89.76,
      359.52,
      96.96
     ],
     "text": "recombination."
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "Morphology \u2014 See comparison tables.\n\u2018Natsukaze\u2019 is a perennial tetraploid (2n = 32) erect\ngrowing guinea grass. Its reproduction is 85%\napomictic \u2014 that is, producing seed without sexual\nrecombination.",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    296.64,
    106.56,
    509.76,
    213.6
   ],
   "id": "e5",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      296.64,
      106.56,
      504.0,
      114.72
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Natsukaze\u2019 is distinct from \u2018Gatton\u2019 in being more"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      296.64,
      116.16,
      493.92,
      124.8
     ],
     "text": "robust and broader leafed than \u2018Gatton\u2019, having"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      296.64,
      125.76,
      495.84,
      134.88
     ],
     "text": "denser and shorter leaf sheath pubescence than"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      296.64,
      136.32,
      474.72,
      144.96
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Gatton\u2019 and having pubescent stem nodes"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      296.64,
      145.92,
      480.0,
      155.04
     ],
     "text": "compared to the glabrous nodes of \u2018Gatton\u2019."
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      296.64,
      155.52,
      494.4,
      164.16
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Natsukaze\u2019 is also distinct from \u2018Petrie\u2019 in being"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      296.64,
      163.68,
      483.36,
      177.6
     ],
     "text": "more robust and broader leafed than \u2018Petrie\u2019,"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      297.12,
      175.68,
      509.76,
      184.8
     ],
     "text": "having a later heading date than \u2018Petrie\u2019 and having"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      296.64,
      185.76,
      493.92,
      194.88
     ],
     "text": "glabrous bright green leaf blade upper surfaces"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      296.64,
      195.84,
      508.8,
      204.96
     ],
     "text": "compared to the pale green finely pubescent upper"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      297.12,
      206.4,
      392.64,
      213.6
     ],
     "text": "leaf surfaces of \u2018Petrie\u2019."
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "\u2018Natsukaze\u2019 is distinct from \u2018Gatton\u2019 in being more\nrobust and broader leafed than \u2018Gatton\u2019, having\ndenser and shorter leaf sheath pubescence than\n\u2018Gatton\u2019 and having pubescent stem nodes\ncompared to the glabrous nodes of \u2018Gatton\u2019.\n\u2018Natsukaze\u2019 is also distinct from \u2018Petrie\u2019 in being\nmore robust and broader leafed than \u2018Petrie\u2019,\nhaving a later heading date than \u2018Petrie\u2019 and having\nglabrous bright green leaf blade upper surfaces\ncompared to the pale green finely pubescent upper\nleaf surfaces of \u2018Petrie\u2019.",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
  {
